WEBVTT

01:32.919 --> 01:36.589
Today we are celebrating
the glorious first birthday

01:36.589 --> 01:38.691
of our beloved Price Belzebuette.

01:38.691 --> 01:41.785
And now for the climax
of our ceremony!

01:43.496 --> 01:44.861
Watch closely everyone!

01:46.098 --> 01:48.267
And now, according to tradition,
his majesty presents

01:48.267 --> 01:51.037
the crown of the capital of Corpus
to the proper heir to the throne.

01:51.037 --> 01:54.040
What a momentous and
glorious occasion!

01:54.040 --> 01:55.803
Everyone please, show the royal family
how happy you are for them!

01:57.677 --> 02:04.515
We wish you the best of luck,
Prince Belzebuette!

02:05.751 --> 02:09.915
And now, the cake to help the
Corpus capital celebrate.

02:10.256 --> 02:12.858
Everyone, you can see Prince
Belzebuette from the window.

02:12.858 --> 02:15.759
Now, the flame atop the Candle Tower
will be blown out.

02:19.265 --> 02:21.334
This is the well-known ritual in which
the voice of our little one

02:21.334 --> 02:24.997
is amplified with the Flute
of the Country Wind.

02:25.504 --> 02:28.140
With the sounding of this special
Flute of the Country Wind,

02:28.140 --> 02:30.610
it is said that the our
magnificent prince

02:30.610 --> 02:32.510
is simultaneously blowing out
the raging fires of Hell.

02:33.746 --> 02:36.180
All right, Price Belzebuette,
are you ready!?

02:42.755 --> 02:47.026
We have been receiving
reports as of late

02:47.026 --> 02:50.696
that a certain Bandit King may be
coming to disturb out ceremony

02:50.696 --> 02:52.721
and to steal the heirlooms of our
country, but he has yet to...

02:58.137 --> 02:59.604
Happy birthday!

03:00.806 --> 03:02.364
There he is! Get him!

03:02.942 --> 03:04.409
Grab him!

03:04.910 --> 03:06.844
Could this really be the Bandit King?

03:10.716 --> 03:14.675
How do I look, Jing?
You like me as a prince?

03:15.054 --> 03:16.919
Not too bad. What are you going
to do with your kingdom?

03:17.156 --> 03:19.488
Oh yeah, all hail King Kir!

03:20.126 --> 03:22.526
How'd you like to try on his crown?

03:23.362 --> 03:26.263
Oh, that one's king size,
I don't think it'd fit me.

03:42.248 --> 03:46.912
The Eternal City of Revaiva
Part 1

03:55.528 --> 03:56.995
Whoops...

03:59.065 --> 04:01.090
We should be all right.

04:03.069 --> 04:04.536
Stick 'em up!

04:04.904 --> 04:06.806
You guys better get out of the way.

04:06.806 --> 04:08.171
You're in my way!

04:09.909 --> 04:11.501
Oh, I'm sorry, did I surprise you?

04:13.512 --> 04:15.247
I just lost my breath.

04:15.247 --> 04:18.341
Well then, my name is Vermouth.

04:21.320 --> 04:22.912
Hey, today is your lucky day.

04:23.522 --> 04:24.989
Check this out.

04:27.326 --> 04:31.330
It says, "Left over from
the days of Arthur

04:31.330 --> 04:34.066
is the key to per lustrate
the acrobat snake,

04:34.066 --> 04:36.967
who stole the lips of the old woman
sleeping in the forest.

04:37.403 --> 04:39.496
It is then that the unending
journey begins."

04:40.039 --> 04:42.708
I only have one life!

04:42.708 --> 04:44.699
I don't want to use it all on
an unending journey!

04:45.711 --> 04:47.838
Hey, the more I look at you,
the cuter you get!

04:48.247 --> 04:48.948
Oh, really?

04:48.948 --> 04:52.213
Well, how'd you like your one life
to be bumped up to 100 or 200?

04:52.752 --> 04:54.820
I know the answer to
the age old question

04:54.820 --> 04:56.583
of how to achieve everlasting life.

04:56.989 --> 05:00.493
Everlasting life?
You mean never dying?

05:00.493 --> 05:01.960
Don't be stupid.

05:02.395 --> 05:06.599
No, a long time ago there was a city
by the name of Revaiva,

05:06.599 --> 05:09.067
where people studied how to escape
old age, sickness and death.

05:09.902 --> 05:12.496
If the legends are really true...

05:18.644 --> 05:20.475
For eternity?

05:23.616 --> 05:26.118
What do you say? You guys
want to get rich with me

05:26.118 --> 05:30.054
selling the secret of eternal life?
Sounds good, doesn't it?!

05:30.756 --> 05:32.892
This sounds good and all but,

05:32.892 --> 05:34.951
where did find out about
all of this, Vermouth?

05:36.295 --> 05:40.163
And exactly why is that you are so
eager to share your good fortune?

05:40.666 --> 05:43.202
Don't you think a treasure this
big will be far too heavy for

05:43.202 --> 05:45.193
a little girl like me to lug around
all by herself?

05:46.539 --> 05:48.803
Something just doesn't seem
right about all of this.

05:53.012 --> 05:54.547
Hey, Jing.

05:54.547 --> 05:56.014
Yo, Postino.

05:56.515 --> 06:00.007
Do you ever deliver letters to towns
that aren't even on the map?

06:00.453 --> 06:01.920
That's my job.

06:02.755 --> 06:04.824
One of these days, I would
just love to try and steal

06:04.824 --> 06:08.157
that incredible map of the world you've
got stowed away in your brain.

06:08.994 --> 06:11.019
It's not a treasure that
can be stolen, Jing.

06:11.497 --> 06:13.365
The geography, towns and people
of this world

06:13.365 --> 06:14.832
are constantly changing, so...

06:15.401 --> 06:17.562
Well, I guess I'd steal a little
from you everyday.

06:18.003 --> 06:20.699
Anyway, have you ever heard
of a city called Revaiva?

06:21.240 --> 06:24.777
Yeah, but not a single letter
has been sent from there,

06:24.777 --> 06:27.211
not even a notice of a death.

06:32.852 --> 06:35.354
So our love really can
thrive for eternity!

06:35.354 --> 06:36.878
For the rest of time...

06:37.590 --> 06:39.391
I can't wait! Let's go, Jing!

06:39.391 --> 06:40.915
We better get on our way then.

06:45.598 --> 06:49.227
Perhaps that little girl really knows
the way to Revaiva?

06:50.936 --> 06:52.403
Let's go, China Lilet!

07:14.193 --> 07:16.161
Are we there yet?

07:16.695 --> 07:18.162
A little bit further.

07:23.135 --> 07:24.727
I thought we were almost there?

07:25.571 --> 07:26.906
Almost.

07:26.906 --> 07:29.375
You've been saying that for
the past two hours now.

07:29.375 --> 07:30.865
Is that right?

07:31.277 --> 07:35.347
Hey, Jing, I thought she was
just a weak little girl,

07:35.347 --> 07:38.717
but it turns out that little body
of hers is pretty strong.

07:38.717 --> 07:40.184
I guess so.

07:52.398 --> 07:53.990
I'm so tired!

07:54.733 --> 07:57.036
I don't think I can go any further.

07:57.036 --> 07:58.604
I have a feeling this place
has something to do with

07:58.604 --> 08:00.663
the "days of Arthur" line
from the riddle.

08:01.674 --> 08:03.375
This looks like an ancient battlefield.

08:03.375 --> 08:06.776
A bunch of stupid people fought here
for some stupid reason.

08:07.146 --> 08:08.681
Maybe it means we should
try and be like Arthur

08:08.681 --> 08:11.081
and pull these swords
from the ground.

08:11.684 --> 08:15.120
If we find Arthur's sword, we'll be
one step closer to eternal life.

08:15.120 --> 08:17.022
We've got to find Excalibur.

08:17.022 --> 08:18.489
But which one is it?

08:19.158 --> 08:21.360
What filthy scum! They look like
your everyday grave robbers.

08:21.360 --> 08:24.591
They couldn't be on the lofty
quest for Excalibur.

08:25.898 --> 08:28.601
You have no respect for the
sacred city of Revaiva

08:28.601 --> 08:31.399
and the legend of their Water
of Unending Life.

08:31.804 --> 08:35.240
I don't suppose you are trying to
find it to make yourselves rich?

08:35.908 --> 08:37.276
Water of Unending Life?

08:37.276 --> 08:39.301
Jing, what's he talking about?

08:40.145 --> 08:41.612
I don't know.

08:41.981 --> 08:45.050
Well, I seriously doubt that your
greedy eyes will be able to find

08:45.050 --> 08:47.917
the true, pure sword that King Arthur
himself once held.

08:48.754 --> 08:50.255
I, Pernod, with my superior eyes,

08:50.255 --> 08:51.757
will be the only one who is
capable of seeing the truth.

08:51.757 --> 08:55.853
Now it is time to find it.
Let's go, China Lilet!

08:56.428 --> 08:58.055
Hey, we've got to hurry!

09:04.903 --> 09:06.495
Oh, what a beautiful aura
this one gives off.

09:07.072 --> 09:09.208
This must be it! I'm sure of it!

09:09.208 --> 09:11.335
I have found it! Pull it up, China Lilet!
It shall be ours!

09:12.978 --> 09:14.468
Jing, have you found it yet?

09:15.614 --> 09:17.249
Could this be it?

09:17.249 --> 09:19.547
C'mon, Jing, don't joke around!

09:19.918 --> 09:21.385
Are you serious?

09:21.954 --> 09:27.153
It's just like you little rats to pick
a shabby sword like that!

09:32.531 --> 09:34.066
What the hell?!

09:34.066 --> 09:36.000
Take care of him, China Lilet!

10:03.095 --> 10:06.298
What a horrible sword, looks like
it's seen one too many battles!

10:06.298 --> 10:10.098
So those dents and stuff on that
sword are there on purpose?

10:10.402 --> 10:13.030
That's right, this is just
a big, oversized key.

10:13.605 --> 10:16.301
That thing's eye looked
like a big keyhole,

10:16.542 --> 10:18.908
and it turned out to be
his on/off switch.

10:19.178 --> 10:20.579
You're right.

10:20.579 --> 10:23.282
It looks like Arthur's Key

10:23.282 --> 10:26.911
was never a gaudy sword like that
with all those jewels.

10:28.120 --> 10:29.888
Of course, you're right.

10:29.888 --> 10:31.480
What he said...

10:38.063 --> 10:39.998
Hey! Where is he taking us?

10:39.998 --> 10:41.465
I don't know.

10:42.101 --> 10:46.060
Maybe, just maybe, he is showing us
they way we need to go.

10:46.739 --> 10:49.041
That would be great.
This guy has made my day!

10:49.041 --> 10:51.236
It looks like he's going to take
care of everything.

11:03.422 --> 11:05.322
Ah, the luster of the white
moonlight in the forest...

11:06.291 --> 11:08.156
The sweet whisper of the woods...

11:14.032 --> 11:15.659
From under the shadows
of the leaves...

11:18.003 --> 11:20.172
Oh, the woman I love...

11:20.172 --> 11:22.936
Even while you sleep, you're the
master of my heart, sweet Vermouth.

11:24.276 --> 11:27.346
I will never tire of you,
my love will never sleep.

11:27.346 --> 11:28.847
Jing is fast asleep.

11:28.847 --> 11:31.816
And I wonder where the hell
this guy is really taking us?

11:32.918 --> 11:36.615
I'm excited, but scared. Our future
lies in this guy's hands.

11:39.491 --> 11:42.187
Jing! Jing! I see something. Hey, Jing!

12:00.979 --> 12:04.005
I wonder if this has anything to do
with the second part of the riddle?

12:17.563 --> 12:19.292
What in the world is all this?

12:23.969 --> 12:29.675
I guess next we have to per
lustrate the acrobat snake.

12:29.675 --> 12:33.702
Perselate? Lepumestate? Pepuspate?

12:35.681 --> 12:40.175
To per lustrate! It means
to inspect with care!

12:40.853 --> 12:42.821
You guys aren't very sophisticated,

12:42.821 --> 12:44.721
but you sure do react
to danger quickly.

12:45.858 --> 12:47.593
If you guys really seek the truth,

12:47.593 --> 12:50.494
you must acquaint yourselves with
the classics and the proper study.

12:50.963 --> 12:55.093
You look like a bunch of stupid,
little kids walking around lost.

12:57.769 --> 13:01.535
The acrobat snake exists
inside this very wall.

13:01.840 --> 13:06.334
I should be able to make out the
form of the snake fairly easily.

13:06.879 --> 13:08.346
What are you talking about?

13:08.647 --> 13:11.047
I get it! The language is like a code.

13:11.416 --> 13:15.750
The body of an acrobat can twist
around exactly like a snake's.

13:17.055 --> 13:18.924
Kids like you could have
never solved this riddle.

13:18.924 --> 13:20.915
You only wish you were
as smart as me.

13:22.661 --> 13:25.764
I see, this is it! I see the shape
of this truly acrobatic bone.

13:25.764 --> 13:27.231
This must be it!

13:27.966 --> 13:29.593
Just as the riddle states!

13:32.571 --> 13:36.642
Hey, is it time yet? My arms
are falling asleep.

13:36.642 --> 13:38.337
What's going on?! What's
the meaning of this?

13:38.810 --> 13:40.445
What kind of sign is this?

13:40.445 --> 13:45.178
This is not how it should be.
What the?! The acrobat snake!

13:45.918 --> 13:47.419
Are these snake bones over here?

13:47.419 --> 13:50.081
Brain snake, come on!

13:57.129 --> 14:01.896
What fragile bones. One little
disruption caused such a fracture.

14:02.234 --> 14:05.761
Hey, Jing! They've ruined the only
clue we have to finding the city!

14:06.171 --> 14:08.540
That snake was supposed
to show us the way

14:08.540 --> 14:10.872
to the eternal paradise,
but now it's gone!

14:11.376 --> 14:12.811
Yeah, but that wasn't the snake
we're looking for.

14:12.811 --> 14:15.177
The acrobat snake is right here.

14:19.251 --> 14:20.519
The snake is this rope,

14:20.519 --> 14:22.316
and you complete the acrobat
image when you grab it.

14:22.854 --> 14:25.724
The people of the ancient city of
Revaiva must have used knots

14:25.724 --> 14:28.625
as a way of recording
time and history.

14:29.261 --> 14:34.399
For example, this is friendship,
this is hard work, and this is...

14:34.399 --> 14:35.567
Is it victory?

14:35.567 --> 14:37.125
Nope, athlete's foot.

14:37.769 --> 14:40.966
On the other side, must lay
a deep, green forest.

14:41.273 --> 14:44.208
In the middle of which, I'm guessing
we'll find an old lady.

14:45.143 --> 14:48.112
I wonder if we'll ever
make it all the way?

14:48.847 --> 14:50.549
The old lady of the sleeping forest

14:50.549 --> 14:53.814
must be waiting for us in the
middle of the forest, right?

14:54.586 --> 14:55.754
I think so.

14:55.754 --> 14:58.416
I have no idea what you guys
are talking about really.

14:59.124 --> 15:00.716
You must keep an open mind when
reading riddles like this.

15:01.259 --> 15:03.386
Don't take the words so literally

15:03.862 --> 15:06.264
and the line of understanding
will never be cut.

15:06.264 --> 15:09.927
Oh, I understand now! You want me
to cut the rope!

15:11.403 --> 15:13.098
Good luck, Jing!

15:14.139 --> 15:16.164
I thought this was part of the plan.

15:17.342 --> 15:19.207
He's heavier than he looks.

15:19.611 --> 15:21.380
Now is no time for a nap.

15:21.380 --> 15:26.443
That old lady in the forest is waiting
for a kiss from you two.

15:30.322 --> 15:33.155
Is this the forest the rope spoke of?

15:33.692 --> 15:34.526
Maybe.

15:34.526 --> 15:36.261
What's this house doing here?

15:36.261 --> 15:38.196
Maybe this is where the beautiful
girl of the forest lives!

15:38.196 --> 15:41.222
Dang, I forgot! She supposed
to be old, not beautiful!

15:41.700 --> 15:44.430
I'd rather die than kiss an old lady.

15:45.537 --> 15:47.334
Anyway, let's just check out
the inside.

15:47.873 --> 15:51.639
Excuse me, may I help you?

15:52.778 --> 15:55.770
Oh, I hope this is her. I could
give her a million kisses!

15:57.115 --> 15:58.517
What is it?

15:58.517 --> 16:00.485
We are looking for someone,

16:01.119 --> 16:02.950
I don't suppose you know an old
lady that lives around here?

16:03.321 --> 16:05.312
Is this truly what it means
to rest in peace?

16:06.758 --> 16:10.956
There used to be an old lady here,
but that was many years ago.

16:11.763 --> 16:16.168
Well, does that mean that we can try
to steal this girl's lips instead?

16:16.168 --> 16:17.402
That won't work!
Well, does that mean that we can try
to steal this girl's lips instead?

16:17.402 --> 16:17.736
That won't work!

16:17.736 --> 16:20.539
Yes, but it's not like we go around
kissing tombstones!

16:20.539 --> 16:22.340
That doesn't mean you get
to kiss this girl!

16:22.340 --> 16:23.842
You'll have to wait until she grows old.

16:23.842 --> 16:24.209
By the time that happens
I'll be six feet under.
You'll have to wait until she grows old.

16:24.209 --> 16:26.973
By the time that happens
I'll be six feet under.

16:28.713 --> 16:30.916
There's no other shelter around here,

16:30.916 --> 16:32.551
so feel free to stay here if you like.

16:32.551 --> 16:37.222
Oh, thank you. We haven't
eaten since morning.

16:37.222 --> 16:40.521
I can't go on any longer. Please
give me something to eat.

16:47.866 --> 16:51.700
You got it? I know you can
deliver this report.

16:52.170 --> 16:53.637
I'm counting on you.

16:55.640 --> 16:57.130
You never seem to rest, do you?

16:57.676 --> 16:59.244
What do you mean?

16:59.244 --> 17:02.881
Kir says that since you aren't
tired, maybe you...

17:02.881 --> 17:04.678
What are you trying to say?!

17:05.383 --> 17:09.054
By the way, I already found
the sleeping old lady.

17:09.054 --> 17:11.215
What? Where? Where is she?!

17:11.990 --> 17:14.652
The moon will soon be coming
through the clouds.

17:15.193 --> 17:17.093
Once that happens, she will
make her appearance.

17:17.696 --> 17:20.494
But that girl said that no one else
lives around he...

17:23.168 --> 17:24.635
Here she comes.

17:33.912 --> 17:37.040
You're saying that those
mountains are her face.

17:41.419 --> 17:44.354
I think even Kir could steal those lips.

17:49.394 --> 17:51.225
What are you guys doing up so late?

17:51.696 --> 17:53.163
I'm no owl, you know.
I can't see well at night.

17:53.598 --> 17:55.065
Kir, let's go.

17:55.500 --> 17:56.967
Where are we going?

17:58.069 --> 18:00.333
To steal the lips of the old woman
sleeping in the forest.

18:00.605 --> 18:02.630
It is then that the unending
journey begins.

18:04.442 --> 18:08.503
I guess just by coming here
we're stealing her lips.

18:09.347 --> 18:11.983
So what's next? The unending
journey begins?

18:11.983 --> 18:14.719
Do we get some kind of prize
for figuring this all out?

18:14.719 --> 18:16.186
What's it going to be?
Who will give it to us?

18:17.155 --> 18:19.591
Hey, Jing, what did the rope letters
say about this?

18:19.591 --> 18:21.582
I think we'll figure it out soon enough.

18:28.133 --> 18:30.602
I drink and drink and it never empties.

18:30.602 --> 18:33.867
There's always more, and I never
even get drunk.

18:42.080 --> 18:44.716
I can drink until the end of the ages

18:44.716 --> 18:47.241
and this wine will never disappear!

18:50.121 --> 18:51.588
Who the hell are you?!

18:53.358 --> 18:55.155
We're just passing through.

18:55.694 --> 18:58.094
Visitors? Passing through?

18:58.663 --> 19:03.301
No one is allowed to see me serving
my drunken, eternal sentence!

19:03.301 --> 19:05.064
He's going to kill us all!

19:06.905 --> 19:09.339
There's no place for us to go!

19:14.012 --> 19:16.514
He's got to have a weakness,
just like anyone else.

19:16.514 --> 19:19.005
Let's try Kir Royale!

19:27.025 --> 19:28.492
Over here old man!

19:33.732 --> 19:35.634
I think one shot should do
the trick, right, Kir?

19:35.634 --> 19:37.369
Don't hit him in the waist.

19:37.369 --> 19:39.769
Since when do you worry about
how bad our enemies get hurt?!

19:41.039 --> 19:42.506
Kir Royale!

19:43.275 --> 19:44.799
It's no good. It passed
right through him.

20:03.128 --> 20:06.495
Thank you, I am finally free,

20:08.066 --> 20:12.127
free from my eternal prison
of that alcohol.

20:13.638 --> 20:15.162
I want to thank you, little one.

20:18.677 --> 20:20.278
Now I can finally get some rest.

20:20.278 --> 20:22.041
It's been over 2,000 years
since I last slept.

20:24.149 --> 20:27.380
I don't know much, but he sure does
look happy now.

20:28.119 --> 20:30.644
All that old man wanted to do
was get some sleep.

20:31.389 --> 20:33.380
He would never have been able
to finish all that wine.

20:35.894 --> 20:40.092
Drinking and drinking the wine,
without rest or reward.

20:40.498 --> 20:43.058
He'd been living his life in that daze
for so long.

20:43.435 --> 20:45.303
What are you talking about, Vermouth?

20:45.303 --> 20:46.770
Jing?

20:47.305 --> 20:48.772
What's that, some kind of vehicle?

20:49.607 --> 20:51.507
Where are we supposed
to go from here?

20:54.312 --> 20:56.280
I think we'll find our answer
blowing in the wind.

20:56.648 --> 20:58.582
In the wind?

21:02.787 --> 21:04.222
It's a boat?

21:04.222 --> 21:05.712
What a crazy drunk.

21:09.361 --> 21:10.828
It's starting to rain.

21:11.496 --> 21:13.631
This umbrella is perfect for the
both of us, right, Vermouth?

21:13.631 --> 21:17.089
So is this what is meant by the
unending journey beginning?

21:18.970 --> 21:20.597
Nope, I think you're a little off.

21:25.610 --> 21:27.805
Kir, Vermouth, let's go!
